[36m(RolloutManager pid=12081)[0m [2026-09-29 04:41:50.801 rollout_manager] sglang_rollout.py:494 - Finish rollout: ['<|im_start|>user\nTim rides his bike back and forth to work for each of his 5 workdays.  His work is 20 miles away.  He also goes for a weekend bike ride of 200 miles.    If he can bike at 25 mph how much time does he spend biking a week?\nPut the final numeric answer in \\boxed{}.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\nWe are told the following information:\n\n- Tim rides his bike **back and forth** every **5 workdays**.\n- His **work distance** is **20 miles per day**.\n- He also goes on a **weekend bike ride** of **200 miles per day**.\n- His biking speed is **25 miles per hour**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Find total distance biking per day\n\nTim travels:\n- 20 miles/day (work trip)\n- 200 miles (weekend trip)\n\nSo, **total biking distance per day is**:\n\n$$\n20 \\text{ miles} + 200 \\text{ miles} = 220 \\text{ miles per day}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Find total biking distance per week\n\nHe travels **5 workdays** and one weekend day. So:\n\n$$\n220 \\text{ miles/day} \\times 5 \\text{ workdays} + 200 \\text{ miles} = 1100 \\text{ miles (work trips)} + 200 \\text{ miles (weekend ride)} = 1300 \\text{ miles}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Calculate time biking in hours\n\nWe know speed is 25 mph, so time = distance / speed:\n\n$$\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{1300 \\text{ miles}}{25 \\text{ mph}} = 52 \\text{ hours}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{52} \\text{ hours}\n$$<|im_end|>'], label: 16, reward: 0.0
